When some eigenvalues are complex, a more interpretable basis in which to analyse the dynamics is given by the real Schur decomposition A = QT Q⊺, where Q and T are real-valued matrices, with Q−1 = Q⊺ (i.e., Q is an orthogonal matrix) and T a block upper-triangular matrix


T=(B1Ω12Ω13…Ω1K0B2Ω23…Ω2K⋮⋮⋮⋱⋮00…BK−1ΩK−1,K00…0BK)
