\begin{document}$$\displaystyle \begin{gathered}X=\left[\begin{array}{cccc}\mathbf{x}^{(1)}(1) & \mathbf{x}^{(2)}(1) & \ldots & \mathbf{x}^{(K)}(1) \\ \mathbf{x}^{(1)}(2) & \mathbf{x}^{(2)}(2) & \ldots & \mathbf{x}^{(K)}(2) \\ \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\ \mathbf{x}^{(1)}(T) & \mathbf{x}^{(2)}(T) & \ldots & \mathbf{x}^{(K)}(T)\end{array}\right], \\ F=\left[\begin{array}{cccc}f_{1}\left(\theta^{(1)}\right) & f_{1}\left(\theta^{(2)}\right) & \ldots & f_{1}\left(\theta^{(K)}\right) \\ f_{2}\left(\theta^{(1)}\right) & f_{2}\left(\theta^{(2)}\right) & \ldots & f_{2}\left(\theta^{(K)}\right) \\ \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots \\ f_{P}\left(\theta^{(1)}\right) & f_{P}\left(\theta^{(2)}\right) & \ldots & f_{P}\left(\theta^{(K)}\right) \\ 1 & 1 & \ldots & 1\end{array}\right], \\ W=\left[\begin{array}{ccccc}\mathbf{w}_{1}(1) & \mathbf{w}_{2}(1) & \ldots & \mathbf{w}_{P}(1) & \mathbf{w}_{0}(1) \\ \mathbf{w}_{1}(2) & \mathbf{w}_{2}(2) & \ldots & \mathbf{w}_{P}(2) & \mathbf{w}_{0}(2) \\ \vdots & \vdots & \ddots & \vdots & \vdots \\ \mathbf{w}_{1}(T) & \mathbf{w}_{2}(T) & \ldots & \mathbf{w}_{P}(T) & \mathbf{w}_{0}(T)\end{array}\right]\end{gathered}$$\end{document}

To solve for fp(θ) given estimates of wp(t), note that:
X¯=W:,1:PF¯1:P,:+W01⊤ \begin{document}$$\displaystyle \bar{X}=W_{:, 1: P} \bar{F}_{1: P,:}+W_{0} \mathbf{1}^{\top}$$\end{document}
where X¯∈RNT×Nstim\begin{document}$\bar{X} \in \mathbb{R}^{N T \times N_{\text {stim }}}$\end{document} contains the PSTHs ⟨x(k)(t)⟩stim(k)=θ,F¯p,θ=fp(θ)\begin{document}$\left\langle\mathbf{x}^{(k)}(t)\right\rangle_{\operatorname{stim}(k)=\theta}, \bar{F}_{p, \theta}=f_{p}(\theta)$\end{document} and 1∈RNstim\begin{document}$\mathbf{1} \in \mathbb{R}^{N_{\text {stim }}}$\end{document} is a vector of ones (with 1 ≤ θ ≤ Nstim the stimulus labels). Thus, we obtain F¯1:P,:=W+(X¯−W01⊤)\begin{document}$\bar{F}_{1: P,:}=W^{+}\left(\bar{X}-W_{0} \mathbf{1}^{\boldsymbol{\top}}\right)$\end{document}. To fit the TDR model to data, we iterated between these two updates until convergence, initialising with fp(θ) ∼ N(0, 1) (for 1 ≤ p ≤ P and 1 ≤ θ ≤ Nstim).
